# Requests against a locally running catalog service (`pnpm nx serve catalog`).
# Run them with the REST Client extension in VS Code (humao.rest-client) or the
# HTTP Client in JetBrains IDEs: click "Send Request" above a request.
# The same endpoints are in Swagger UI: http://localhost:3000/docs

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Liveness: is the process up? (never checks the database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness: can it serve requests? (checks the database; 503 when Postgres is down)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Barcode lookup: GET /v1/foods/barcode/{code}
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Alpro almond drink: imported from the Open Food Facts export (not tagged Poland)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/5411188110835
Accept-Language: en

### Finuu butter, with a Russian UI: no Russian name, so the Polish one is shown
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/5900012005947
Accept-Language: ru-RU,ru;q=0.9,en;q=0.8

### Finuu with a digit missing: 400, the check digit doesn't match
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/590012005947

### Optimum Nutrition whey: not in the export; the first scan fetches it from the
### Open Food Facts API and stores it, later scans are database hits (compare the times)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/5060751998501

### Not a barcode at all: 400 with the invalid field
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/abc

### A valid barcode nobody has (EAN-8 example): 404; Open Food Facts isn't asked
### again for a day
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/96385074

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Search: GET /v1/foods?q=...&limit=20&offset=0
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Polish, without Polish characters
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=twarog wiejski&limit=5

### A partly typed word
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=serek wiej&limit=5

### A typo
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=mlekko&limit=5

### Russian: products sold in Poland with Russian names come first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=творог&limit=5
Accept-Language: ru

### A very common word: the slowest kind of query (every match is scored)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=whey protein&limit=5

### The next page: pass the previous response's nextOffset as offset
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=mleko&limit=5&offset=5

### Too short: 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods?q=a

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docs and errors
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### The OpenAPI description (JSON)
GET {{baseUrl}}/docs/openapi.json

### An unknown route: 404 as RFC 9457 problem details (application/problem+json)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nothing-here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Custom foods (needs AUTH_MODE=dev-headers in apps/services/catalog/.env)
# Until Phase 2 brings logins, X-Dev-User-Id says who you are (any UUID)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@me = 0192f8a4-6a3e-7c00-8f00-00000000e90e

### Add a private food (only you see it). Copy the id from the response for the next ones
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "names": { "pl": "Mój twarożek", "ru": "Мой творожок" },
  "brand": "Domowe",
  "barcode": "5012345678900",
  "per100": { "kcal": 120, "protein": 14, "fat": 5, "carbs": 3.5 },
  "servings": [{ "label": "1 łyżka (30 g)", "amount": 30 }]
}

### Read it back (anyone else gets 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/{{created.response.body.id}}
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Accept-Language: ru

### Scan its barcode: your food comes first
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/barcode/5012345678900
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}

### Add it again: 409 with existingFoodId
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": { "pl": "Duplikat" }, "barcode": "5012345678900", "per100": { "kcal": 100 } }

### Public needs the contributor role: 403 (add "X-Dev-Roles: contributor" to allow it)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "names": { "pl": "Dla wszystkich" }, "per100": { "kcal": 100 }, "visibility": "public" }

### Change your food (full replacement)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/{{created.response.body.id}}
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "names": { "pl": "Mój twarożek light" },
  "barcode": "5012345678900",
  "per100": { "kcal": 95, "protein": 15, "fat": 2, "carbs": 3.5 }
}

### Retire it: 204; still readable by id, no longer in lookups and search
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/foods/{{created.response.body.id}}
X-Dev-User-Id: {{me}}
